      "side": 1,
      "message": "This breaks the KMI. It seems like we only need to find 1 bit in this struct to do this in a KMI compliant way (you can\u0027t use the KABI fields at the end since they are reserved for LTS updates). Maybe take the MSB of `ll_open_count`? and then have get/set inline functions:\n```\nvoid hdev_set_battery_charge_status(hdev)\n__s32 hdev_get_battery_charge_status(hdev)\n\n\n```\n\nIf you use a bit in ll_open_count, you need to either use accessor functions like below for the inc/decs of `hdev-\u003ell_open_count`:\n```\nunsigned int hdev_inc_ll_open_count(hdev)\nunsigned int hdev_dev_ll_open_count(hdev)\n```\nor you could do some declaration magic to cleanly differentiate the battery bit from the open_count.",
